%e A401152 Examples illustrating row n = 7:
%e A401152   k = 1: 123456 is an even permutation, so T(7,1) = 1;
%e A401152   k = 2: 246135 is an even permutation, so T(7,2) = 1;
%e A401152   k = 3: 362514 is an odd permutation, so T(7,3) = -1;
%e A401152   k = 4: 415263 is an even permutation, so T(7,4) = 1;
%e A401152   k = 5: 531642 is an odd permutation, so T(7,5) = -1;
%e A401152   k = 6: 654321 is an odd permutation, so T(7,6) = -1.
%o A401152 (PARI) A401152(n,k) = if(n%2==1, kronecker(k,n), if(gcd(k,n)==1, if(n%4==0 && k%4==3, -1, 1), 0))
%Y A401152 Cf. A054521, A215200, A401153 (version with 0 omitted), A402232 (Conrey labels).
